{"abstract":[{"text":"Discord-style session-resume client. Runs as an actor so callers don’t","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"have to worry about thread-safety; you can poke it from your transport","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"task and from the main actor freely.","type":"text"}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ResumeKit\/documentation\/ResumeKit\/SessionCoordinator\/Configuration"],"title":"Structures"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ResumeKit\/documentation\/ResumeKit\/SessionCoordinator\/init(transport:storage:token:clientProperties:configuration:)"],"title":"Initializers"},{"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ResumeKit\/documentation\/ResumeKit\/SessionCoordinator\/events","doc:\/\/ResumeKit\/documentation\/ResumeKit\/SessionCoordinator\/state"]},{"title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ResumeKit\/documentation\/ResumeKit\/SessionCoordinator\/clearSession()","doc:\/\/ResumeKit\/documentation\/ResumeKit\/SessionCoordinator\/connectionDidClose(error:)","doc:\/\/ResumeKit\/documentation\/ResumeKit\/SessionCoordinator\/connectionDidOpen()","doc:\/\/ResumeKit\/documentation\/ResumeKit\/SessionCoordinator\/currentSnapshot()","doc:\/\/ResumeKit\/documentation\/ResumeKit\/SessionCoordinator\/didReceive(_:)"]},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ResumeKit\/documentation\/ResumeKit\/SessionCoordinator\/Actor-Implementations"],"title":"Default Implementations","generated":true}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"actor","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SessionCoordinator","kind":"identifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Architecture","type":"heading","level":1,"anchor":"Architecture"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The coordinator owns three pieces of state:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The in-memory ","type":"text"},{"code":"state","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (handshaking \/ replaying \/ live \/ disconnected)."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A persistent "},{"code":"(sessionId, lastSeq)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" cursor in ","type":"text"},{"code":"SessionStorage","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A heartbeat timer that fires while the connection is healthy.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It does "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"not","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" own the connection itself — that’s your transport’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"problem. The coordinator just decides what to send when you tell it"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"“the connection is open” or “I received this frame”.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Lifecycle (the seven calls you’ll make)","level":1,"anchor":"Lifecycle-the-seven-calls-youll-make","type":"heading"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ 1. On WebSocket connect:","await coordinator.connectionDidOpen()","       \/\/ → coordinator decides Identify vs Resume from storage,","       \/\/   asks transport to send the chosen handshake frame.","","\/\/ 2. On every incoming frame your decoder parses:","await coordinator.didReceive(.ready(sessionId: \"abc\", initialSeq: 0))","await coordinator.didReceive(.pushEvent(seq: 17))","await coordinator.didReceive(.heartbeatAck)","\/\/ ...","","\/\/ 3. On WebSocket close:","await coordinator.connectionDidClose(error: someError)","","\/\/ 4. On user logout:","await coordinator.clearSession()"],"type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"Subscribing-to-events","type":"heading","text":"Subscribing to events","level":1},{"code":["Task {","  for await event in await coordinator.events {","    switch event {","    case .replayStarted:           muteNotifications()","    case .replayFinis